    {
      "id": "02",
      "title": "What sharding costs you",
      "question": "What gets harder once your data is sharded?",
      "scenes": [
        {
          "type": "question",
          "say": "Question two. What gets harder once your data is sharded, and how do you soften each cost? Pause and answer out loud.",
          "pauseAfter": 3,
          "props": {
            "question": "What gets <em>harder</em> once your data is sharded?"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "points",
          "say": "Sharding makes four things harder. Joins across shards turn into slow scatter-gather, so denormalize, or pick a shard key that keeps related rows together, like the tenant ID. Transactions across shards need two-phase commit, or a saga. Rebalancing: with hash mod N, adding a shard moves most rows. And every operation, from backups to schema changes, now runs once per shard.",
          "props": {
            "title": "Four <em>costs</em>",
            "items": [
              {
                "at": "Joins",
                "label": "Cross-shard joins",
                "title": "Co-locate",
                "body": "Shard by tenant_id so related rows live together.",
                "code": "scatter-gather"
              },
              {
                "at": "Transactions",
                "label": "Cross-shard writes",
                "title": "2PC or saga",
                "body": "ACID across shards is slow and fragile.",
                "code": "two-phase commit"
              },
              {
                "at": "Rebalancing",
                "label": "Adding shards",
                "title": "Rows move",
                "body": "hash % N remaps most keys when N changes.",
                "code": "hash % N"
              },
              {
                "at": "operation",
                "label": "Operations",
                "title": "Everything × N",
                "body": "Backups, migrations and monitoring per shard.",
                "code": "ops overhead"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "compare",
          "say": "That rebalancing cost deserves a fix. With hash mod the number of hosts, going from four hosts to five moves about eighty percent of the rows. Instead, pre-split the key space into, say, a thousand and twenty-four logical shards, and map them onto hosts. Adding a host then moves a few whole logical shards, and only the mapping changes.",
          "props": {
            "title": "Move shards, <em>not rows</em>",
            "lang": "python",
            "left": {
              "at": "going",
              "label": "Hash by host count",
              "title": "hash % hosts",
              "tone": "bad",
              "code": "host = hash(key) % 4    # now % 5\n# ~80% of rows move"
            },
            "right": {
              "at": "logical",
              "label": "Logical shards",
              "title": "Fixed shard count",
              "tone": "good",
              "code": "shard = hash(key) % 1024   # never changes\nhost = shard_map[shard]    # edit to move"
            },
            "verdict": {
              "at": "mapping",
              "text": "Fix the shard count; rebalance by moving whole shards.",
              "code": "shard_map"
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "03",
      "title": "When to shard",
      "question": "Your database is struggling. When is sharding actually the right move?",
      "scenes": [
        {
          "type": "question",
          "say": "Question three. Your database is struggling. When is sharding actually the right move? Pause and answer out loud.",
          "pauseAfter": 3,
          "props": {
            "question": "When is sharding <em>actually</em> the right move?"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "points",
          "say": "Sharding is a last resort, so climb the ladder first. Fix slow queries and missing indexes. Scale up to a bigger machine. Offload reads to replicas and a cache. Shard only when writes, or the data itself, outgrow a single primary.",
          "props": {
            "title": "Climb the <em>ladder</em> first",
            "items": [
              {
                "at": "queries",
                "label": "Step 1",
                "title": "Tune",
                "body": "Slow queries, missing indexes.",
                "code": "EXPLAIN"
              },
              {
                "at": "bigger",
                "label": "Step 2",
                "title": "Scale up",
                "body": "More CPU, RAM, faster disks.",
                "code": "vertical"
              },
              {
                "at": "replicas",
                "label": "Step 3",
                "title": "Offload reads",
                "body": "Read replicas and a cache.",
                "code": "reads ≫ writes"
              },
              {
                "at": "outgrow",
                "label": "Step 4",
                "title": "Shard",
                "body": "Writes or data outgrow one primary.",
                "code": "last resort"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "recap",
          "say": "To recap. Hash sharding spreads load, but scatters range queries. Range sharding keeps ranges together, but creates hotspots. A directory is flexible, but adds a hop. Keep related rows on one shard, rebalance with logical shards, and shard only after tuning, scaling up, and replicas.",
          "props": {
            "title": "Sharding, <em>in five lines</em>",
            "items": [
              {
                "at": "spreads",
                "text": "Hash: even load, scattered range queries.",
                "code": "hash(key) % N"
              },
              {
                "at": "hotspots",
                "text": "Range: fast ranges, write hotspots.",
                "code": "order_date"
              },
              {
                "at": "flexible",
                "text": "Directory: flexible, but an extra hop.",
                "code": "key → shard"
              },
              {
                "at": "related",
                "text": "Co-locate related rows; move logical shards.",
                "code": "tenant_id"
              },
              {
                "at": "only",
                "text": "Shard only after tuning, scaling up, replicas.",
                "code": "last resort"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
